- `verified` raises an `Oci.Error` if the bytes disagree with the digest or the size which the
- manifest declares. Checking a stream would mean draining it, which is why `verified` gathers
- the bytes first.
+ `verified` lanza un `Oci.Error` si los bytes no coinciden con el resumen o el tamaño que declara el
+ manifiesto. Comprobar un flujo significaría vaciarlo, y por eso `verified` reúne antes los bytes.

